# Family A29: payload copy modes and zero-copy receive (internal/engine).
# See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/engine
BENCH=BenchmarkMemory/PubSubAck
REF=safe
AUTO_KEY=copymode
KIND_DIM=""
KINDS_TEST=TestCopyModeKindsList
AUTO_FILE=-
ADR=9
TITLE="Payload ownership, copy modes and zero-copy receive (A29)"
# The engine hosts four variant families, so this one has its own list test:
#   hack/bakeoff.sh A29
# Appendix A row A29 is "Safe → all shipped": a copy mode is chosen per
# publication rather than bound at build time, so the bake-off produces a
# report and no binding — AUTO_FILE=- disables the generated auto.go, and
# adr/ADR-009 carries no auto: front-matter for the family. The mode is a path
# segment of the benchmark name rather than a key=value dimension, which is
# why KIND_DIM is empty, and it is the *first* segment after the root: the
# specification spells this one name in two orders — §9.1 row A6 mode first,
# §10.5 concurrency first — and the mode leads because that is the segment
# this script's per-kind filter and `bakeoff decide` both read
# (adr/ADR-017-assumptions.md). The benchmark lives in PKG
# rather than in the nested benchmarks module, where a `go test` run in PKG
# cannot reach it and every per-kind filter selected nothing (assumption
# A24.8); the four slugs are the ones TestCopyModeKindsList prints, and
# `bakeoff lint` fails when one of them has no benchmark.
# The §9
# criterion is throughput against the safe reference at 1P1C, with the
# allocation and gc-cycles columns alongside: the modes trade a copy for an
# ownership rule, so what they cost is what the bake-off is measuring.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="all shipped; safe default (throughput + alias-correctness tests, all must pass)"
# MATRIX=default, deliberately: assumption A24.5 already measured what the
# alternative costs. The default grid is nine rows per arm -- every §10.4
# payload size at 1P1C, and the two ends at 4P4C and 8P8C -- and `full`
# crosses every size with every shape for an hour of a shared host and two
# arms' worth of information. The criterion is throughput plus the
# alias-correctness tests, which are tests and run in the correctness gate.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="1P1C 4P4C 8P8C bytes=64 bytes=65536 reuse=on reuse=off"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op msgs/s bytes/s"
